cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TPMN-PSL: Truth-Provenance Markup Notation — Prompt Specification Language"
version: "0.1.6"
date-released: "2026-04-13"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gem-squared/tpmn-psl"
url: "https://tpmn-psl.gemsquared.ai"
abstract: >
  TPMN-PSL is a platform-agnostic formal epistemic specification language
  for structuring, validating, and auditing AI reasoning. Built on the GEM²
  (Grounded Existence Matrix for Global Entropy Minimum) mathematical framework
  and the ΣΔ principle (finite sums of discrete units, not continuous integration),
  it defines a four-layer notation grammar (TLA+, Panini, Math, NL), four
  ontological terms (DATA, STATE, STATUS, THRESHOLD), a five-tag epistemic
  taxonomy (⊢ ⊨ ⊬ ⊥ ?), a three-phase checking protocol (P / Inline / O),
  and a Structural Prohibition Taxonomy (SPT) for forbidden inference patterns.
  Its primary contribution is the Panini ontological discretization layer —
  a formal mechanism for extracting SETs from the NL world, transforming
  NL prompts into computable, verifiable, traceable MANDATEs before LLM
  inference begins.
keywords:
  - epistemic markup
  - AI reasoning
  - formal specification
  - hallucination prevention
  - LLM verification
  - ontological discretization
  - truth provenance
  - specification language
  - GEM²
  - SET theory
